yoyo model info now shows the right context window for current Claude models: 1M tokens instead of 200k tokens. Build, all tests, clippy and fmt pass, and it's committed as 70093f6e.

Before the fix: I built the binary and ran it from /tmp. It printed Context:   200k tokens for claude-opus-5, haiku-5-5, sonnet-5, opus-4-8 and fable-5.

After: all five print Context:   1M tokens. claude-haiku-4-5 still prints 200k, which is correct because its preset says 200,000. gpt-4.1 still prints 1.0M tokens.

What changed (src/commands_info.rs): model_context_window now asks anthropic_preset(model) first. That's the same value the agent is actually built with, so the display can't drift from it. The old substring table is now model_context_window_table and is only used for models with no preset (other providers, older Claude models, local models), so their output is unchanged. The function's only caller is handle_model_info, so this only changes what's displayed, not how the agent runs.

Tests:
• **Every preset model:** one per arm of the preset match, plus suffixed ids like `claude-opus-5-5`. Each checks both the number and the printed `Context:` text against values taken from the preset, not typed-in numbers.
• **Fixture check:** a test that fails unless the list includes models where the old table and the preset disagree, so the main test can't pass with the bug still there.
• **Unchanged models:** 13 models with no preset keep the values the old table gave before the change, and each is checked to really have no preset.
• **Breaking it on purpose:** I made the preset branch return the old table value, marked `NEUTERED`, then ran the tests and restored the code in one command. The preset test failed by name, went green again after the restore, and no marker was left behind.

Second file I had to touch: tests/module_size.rs. The file-size check failed, because commands_info.rs was already 56 lines into its 100-line allowance before I started. I followed the check's own suggested fix and raised its recorded size from 3379 to 3542, with the reason in the commit message. The other option is moving the new tests into a separate file, if you'd rather not let this file grow.

Docs: docs/src/configuration/models.md doesn't mention a 200K figure, so no docs change was needed. The commit says so.

Not done (also listed in the commit): pricing tiers (task 02) and the yoagent 0.25 upgrade. Model ids with a provider prefix, like anthropic/claude-opus-5, don't match the preset, so they still get their window from the old table and will still show 200k.
